                            "params": {
                                "text": "<h2 id=\"ch1-prose\">Prose</h2>\n<p>None of the dollars on this page is a formula.</p>\n<p>The upgrade costs $5 and the extra module $10 more, so budget $15 in total.</p>\n<p>Export $PATH and $HOME before running it.</p>\n<p>A single escaped pair: $notmath$.</p>\n<p>Inline code keeps its dollars: <code>$x$</code> and <code>$$y$$</code>.</p>\n<div style=\"background-color:#f6f8fa\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\"><span style=\"color:#6f42c1\">echo</span> <span style=\"color:#032f62\">&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#e36209\">$PATH</span><span style=\"color:#032f62\">&quot;\n</span><span style=\"color:#d73a49\">if</span> [ -n <span style=\"color:#032f62\">&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#e36209\">$1</span><span style=\"color:#032f62\">&quot;</span> ]; <span style=\"color:#d73a49\">then</span> <span style=\"color:#6f42c1\">echo</span> <span style=\"color:#032f62\">&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#e36209\">$1</span><span style=\"color:#032f62\">&quot;</span>; <span style=\"color:#d73a49\">fi\n</span></code></pre>\n</div>\n<p>Whitespace just inside the delimiters disqualifies it: $ x $ stays text.</p>\n<p>An unclosed dollar $ on its own is text too, and so is a lone backslash \\ or a [ that never closes.</p>\n"
                            },
